; Woven DNS, for import into Cloudflare
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Cloudflare: your zone > DNS > Records > Import and Export > Import.
; Everything arrives DNS-only (grey cloud), which is what we want. See
; docs/dns/README.md for why, and for what to do after.
;
; The four domains are already registered against their Railway services and
; are waiting on these records; the CNAME targets below came from Railway's
; API, not from a guess.
;
; TTL 300 while things are moving. Raise it to 3600 once the addresses have
; not changed for a week.

$ORIGIN woventechnology.com.
$TTL 300

; --- the site ---------------------------------------------------------------
; Cloudflare flattens a CNAME at the apex, so the bare domain points at Railway
; without an A record whose address we would then have to chase.
@                       300  IN  CNAME  8yqpl9im.up.railway.app.
www                     300  IN  CNAME  w4um6z2s.up.railway.app.

; --- the public API ---------------------------------------------------------
; Reservations, applications and contact. Holds no household data.
api                     300  IN  CNAME  yxc9ldh5.up.railway.app.

; --- the relay --------------------------------------------------------------
; Carries sealed frames between a Core and its dashboards and keeps nothing.
; It must stay DNS-only: the connection is a long-lived WebSocket, and a proxy
; in front of it buys nothing and can time it out mid-session.
relay                   300  IN  CNAME  pnfom1f8.up.railway.app.

; --- proving the domain is ours ---------------------------------------------
; Railway's ownership check. It can usually verify from the CNAME alone, but
; these cost nothing and remove the second round trip if it cannot. They can be
; deleted once every certificate is issued.
_railway-verify         300  IN  TXT    "railway-verify=75f21c2d317ee4e7012b619edb13874dcee700da5904715eb08fc96f9a4eff66"
_railway-verify.www     300  IN  TXT    "railway-verify=040477270e4cbf16fda366bf7aeb666b317468ef9304735bff50e600f8487bb8"
_railway-verify.api     300  IN  TXT    "railway-verify=2872d44aa0a8d33ae798b65d81c67999fafc43715b6850594a902d4b92798ab3"
_railway-verify.relay   300  IN  TXT    "railway-verify=df92e3f8d1ecbcc41a96ee7c70b5e72495ba9dc687bb430e5b143e5b72cb1033"

; --- mail -------------------------------------------------------------------
; No mail is accepted at this domain, and saying so stops the backscatter an
; unconfigured domain attracts.
@                       300  IN  MX     0 .

; Nothing is authorised to send as this domain yet. When Resend is set up,
; replace this with the record Resend gives you and add its DKIM record beside
; it; until then a hard fail is honest and safer than a permissive record
; nobody revisits.
@                       300  IN  TXT    "v=spf1 -all"

; Reject anything that fails, and hear about it. Change the address to one you
; read, or drop the rua tag.
_dmarc                  300  IN  TXT    "v=DMARC1; p=reject; rua=mailto:dmarc@woventechnology.com; aspf=s; adkim=s"

; --- nothing else -----------------------------------------------------------
; No wildcard. A wildcard answers for every name anyone invents, which is how a
; subdomain nobody meant to publish ends up serving something.
